      "content": "The opposition to vouchers often involves legitimate concerns about equity and accountability that go beyond mere political bias; critics argue that diverting public funds to private schools can lead to a \"two-tier\" system where wealthy families are the only ones benefited by the \"choice\" narrative. Specific arguments include the risk that private schools may not adhere to the same rigorous safety or anti-discrimination standards as public institutions, potentially exposing children to an unregulated environment. While partisanship certainly plays a role in the discourse, these are substantive policy debates regarding the responsibility of society to provide equal outcomes for all students rather than just the right to choose among unverified options.",
